"user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T19:43:53-08:00","id":1035009,"title":"","content":"I wonder who from the 1st edition core didn't make the cut for the full write-up to make room for the Council of Bones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T19:56:16-08:00","id":1035018,"title":"","content":"I'm expecting that every Compact and Conspiracy will be <i>mentioned</i>, with perhaps as much as a paragraph each to give a sense of what they're about; but only a few will get several pages worth of material to themselves.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm most curious about 2e's take on the Code. I know how <i>I'd</i> do it; but I'm curious how Monica plans to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:43:33-08:00","id":1035037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035009#post1035009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder who from the 1st edition core didn't make the cut for the full write-up to make room for the Council of Bones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abbey, if I had to guess.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm an idiot. Cheiron, maybe? Especially if they're baddies in Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 01-19-2017, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T21:00:18-08:00","id":1035046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035009#post1035009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder who from the 1st edition core didn't make the cut for the full write-up to make room for the Council of Bones.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I doubt it would happen, its hypothetically possible that none of the original core C&amp;Cs show up. There are enough from the supplements that you could pick a brand new set of cores. Obviously that won't happen, but we could be looking at losing more than one from each category to allow for a new direction in Hunter products.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T22:03:48-08:00","id":1035067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035046#post1035046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I doubt it would happen, its hypothetically possible that none of the original core C&amp;Cs show up. There are enough from the supplements that you could pick a brand new set of cores. Obviously that won't happen, but we could be looking at losing more than one from each category to allow for a new direction in Hunter products.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of the ones from supplements (many of which I love) have more inherently restrictive focuses than the core 6/6 that are important to their themes. The core were intentionally a set with broader uses, even if they had favored prey (vampires for MM, mages for AKD, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T22:27:27-08:00","id":1035077,"title":"","content":"It might be Null Mysteriis, but times now look dark for Abbey fans...<br /> <br /> (There's cool stuff in that outline and they could be moved to a supplement and still awesome, but freaking out is traditional.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T23:04:06-08:00","id":1035099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035037#post1035037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Cheiron, maybe? Especially if they're baddies in Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make a lot of sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T23:17:04-08:00","id":1035101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035046#post1035046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I doubt it would happen, its hypothetically possible that none of the original core C&amp;Cs show up. There are enough from the supplements that you could pick a brand new set of cores. Obviously that won't happen, but we could be looking at losing more than one from each category to allow for a new direction in Hunter products.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that the core 6 do end up being the same as the ones from 1e, minus the two cuts and plus the two new additions, (a pretty big assumptions, to be fair), it would make sense for Cheiron to be the Conspiracy that gets cut if it's showing up in Deviant. By the same token, it would make a lot of sense for Ashwood to be the Compact that gets cut if it's featuring in the Slasher Chronicle chapter. Which I would certainly hope it does, what with the Hunt Club being part of them and all. I would have assumed Ashwood would be the Compact to VASCU's Conspiracy in that chapter, if it hadn't been specified that the Compact was new and as of yet unnamed. So I'm guessing they've gone full black hat. But it's possible the new Compact could be an Abbey offshoot, the rest having been corrupted by the Hunt Club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-20-2017, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T00:20:41-08:00","id":1035113,"title":"","content":"I'm banking on lucifuge being one of the conspiracies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T03:05:45-08:00","id":1035146,"title":"","content":"This looks really good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm excited to learn more.<br /> <br /> Confused about the mentions of Merits and Flaws though, that seems like a very oWoD phrasing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T04:10:39-08:00","id":1035156,"title":"","content":"A fine outline indeed. Personnally, I think the Lucifuge, the loyalist of Thule and AKD will make the cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/8.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/305-kergonan","name":"Kergonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T06:49:27-08:00","id":1035193,"title":"","content":"Hello! Popping in really quick to say that I'm excited to see how enthusiastic y'all are about the corebook. For 2E, I figured out a way to provide seven compacts and seven conspiracies! All conspiracies from the corebook are getting a full splat and, as I mentioned in the outline, we are providing a &quot;history of&quot; section for both and a section to cover every compact and conspiracy that has ever been mentioned. I am also including a &quot;create your own&quot; section for both compacts and conspiracies that will address the systems. For specifics, I am going to address those at a later date in an OpenDev post. Yay!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1870,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","user":"mlvalentine","date":".  Edited: I have not had enough coffee this morning, and I misrepresented my counts. More later! 01-20-2017, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T06:59:12-08:00","id":1035198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035193#post1035193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! Popping in really quick to say that I'm excited to see how enthusiastic y'all are about the corebook. With respect to compacts and conspiracies, in the first edition corebook there were six compacts and five conspiracies. For 2E, I figured out a way to provide seven compacts and seven conspiracies! All conspiracies from the corebook are getting a full splat and, as I mentioned in the outline, we are providing a &quot;history of&quot; section for both and a section to cover every compact and conspiracy that has ever been mentioned. I am also including a &quot;create your own&quot; section for both compacts and conspiracies that will address the systems. For specifics, I am going to address those at a later date in an OpenDev post. Yay!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to hear, particularly with all the cool stuff from Dark Eras and other stuff scattered among 1st ed books. Looking forward to the result!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:08:58-08:00","id":1035200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035193#post1035193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! Popping in really quick to say that I'm excited to see how enthusiastic y'all are about the corebook. With respect to compacts and conspiracies, in the first edition corebook there were six compacts and five conspiracies. For 2E, I figured out a way to provide seven compacts and seven conspiracies! All conspiracies from the corebook are getting a full splat and, as I mentioned in the outline, we are providing a &quot;history of&quot; section for both and a section to cover every compact and conspiracy that has ever been mentioned. I am also including a &quot;create your own&quot; section for both compacts and conspiracies that will address the systems. For specifics, I am going to address those at a later date in an OpenDev post. Yay!</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome to hear! This has me excited already, much like the Mage and Werewolf 2e previews did. If Hunter 2e can do half of what those two books did to me for their gamelines, it will be very successful indeed. And really, there is every possibility it will do more. It is awesome to see that history will continue to be included. <br /> <br /> One non-core book question. You said that your plan is to introduce new writing blood for each Hunter supplement as well. Does that mean there will be periodic Hunter Open Calls, or you will you be dipping into the existing pool of submissions? My instincts would be towards the latter, but I just wanted to clarify since I know there are a number of us on the forums who would be interested in throwing our hats into the ring if we didn't get a chance to for the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:16:24-08:00","id":1035204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035200#post1035200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One non-core book question. You said that your plan is to introduce new writing blood for each Hunter supplement as well. Does that mean there will be periodic Hunter Open Calls, or you will you be dipping into the existing pool of submissions? My instincts would be towards the latter, but I just wanted to clarify since I know there are a number of us on the forums who would be interested in throwing our hats into the ring if we didn't get a chance to for the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to draw on the existing open submissions pile. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:23:47-08:00","id":1035209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035200#post1035200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome to hear! This has me excited already, much like the Mage and Werewolf 2e previews did. If Hunter 2e can do half of what those two books did to me for their gamelines, it will be very successful indeed. And really, there is every possibility it will do more. It is awesome to see that history will continue to be included.</div> </div> </div> </div>No kidding, I really think of the current batch of Chronicles of Darkness as a &quot;golden age&quot; for the genre. All the 2nd edition core books are very strong and with Changeling, Hunter and Geist on the way, I couldn't be more excited. This is going to be a good year!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:46:42-08:00","id":1035220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035018#post1035018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm expecting that every Compact and Conspiracy will be <i>mentioned</i>, with perhaps as much as a paragraph each to give a sense of what they're about; but only a few will get several pages worth of material to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of Monica's replies confirms this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035067#post1035067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the ones from supplements (many of which I love) have more inherently restrictive focuses than the core 6/6 that are important to their themes. The core were intentionally a set with broader uses, even if they had favored prey (vampires for MM, mages for AKD, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>The core compacts mostly showcased reasons to hunt (religious duty, neighbourhood watch, scientific enquiry, thrills), while the core conspiracies showcased types of Endowment (blood-borne power, holy rites, high technology, mystical artefacts), and that seems like a philosophy it would make sense to retain. Anyway, another of Monica's replies confirmed that most in the new core will be retained from the old.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess which one was being relegated, it would be Aegis kai Doru (relics are the easiest Endowment to decouple from a parent conspiracy and make a generic thing hunters can have - and relatedly, the Endowment most logical to have turn up in the hands of other groups like the Malleus Maleficarum, Ascending Ones, or Council of Bones - or for that matter, relics of the dead are a logical Endowment for the Council to have) or Malleus Maleficarum (the other logical option for the Council's Endowment is some sort of ritual necromancy, which would fill the same magical rite niche of Benedictions). If it is one of those, I hope it would be Aegis kai Doru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035101#post1035101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same token, it would make a lot of sense for Ashwood to be the Compact that gets cut if it's featuring in the Slasher Chronicle chapter. Which I would certainly hope it does, what with the Hunt Club being part of them and all. I would have assumed Ashwood would be the Compact to VASCU's Conspiracy in that chapter, if it hadn't been specified that the Compact was new and as of yet unnamed. So I'm guessing they've gone full black hat. But it's possible the new Compact could be an Abbey offshoot, the rest having been corrupted by the Hunt Club.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new compact isn't just unnamed, it's specifically said to be brand new. My hope is it's either formed out of frequently victimised populations (the homeless, sex workers, etc...), or maybe people who support them like social workers or counsellors. A group focussed on supporting the kinds of people slashers and other killers would often be targeting would be a good counterpart to the law enforcement conspiracy - or to put it another way, a Catherine Black to go with VASCU's Frank Black.<br /> <br /> I do agree that it seems Ashwood Abbey would be a logical compact to go. The other one I could see is the Union, since it seems like the easiest to replicate its themes without a specific splat for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:13:46-08:00","id":1035228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035220#post1035220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of Monica's replies confirms this.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess which one was being relegated, it would be Aegis kai Doru (relics are the easiest Endowment to decouple from a parent conspiracy and make a generic thing hunters can have - and relatedly, the Endowment most logical to have turn up in the hands of other groups like the Malleus Maleficarum, Ascending Ones, or Council of Bones - or for that matter, relics of the dead are a logical Endowment for the Council to have) or Malleus Maleficarum (the other logical option for the Council's Endowment is some sort of ritual necromancy, which would fill the same magical rite niche of Benedictions). If it is one of those, I hope it would be Aegis kai Doru.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize for answering this in a blurry haze of uncaffeinated-ness. I'm super excited and focused on the fact that we have seven compacts/conspiracies, and I will have more on this later. Huzzah!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1870,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","user":"mlvalentine","date":". 01-20-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:36:54-08:00","id":1035240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035228#post1035228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned upthread, every conspiracy that was in the HTV1E corebook will also be included in 2nd Edition. No conspiracy is on the &quot;chopping block.&quot; There were five conspiracies in the first edition corebook, and there will be seven in this one. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>There were six: Aegis kai Doru, Ascending Ones, Cheiron Group, Lucifuge, Malleus Maleficarum, and TFV.<br /> <br /> Edited to add: or should I take this to mean that one of them isn't being removed, but altered into a compact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 01-20-2017, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:40:57-08:00","id":1035245,"title":"","content":"Finally! I'm waiting for this for such a long time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although I really fear for the fate of the Abbey now- but again, I have already made them into a conspiracy in my game, meaning I'm way out of canon as far as they are concerned, so such change would hardly effect my games, I think. Other than that, I'm excited to see that Monica did managed to add more splats to the book, and is going to represent all groups in it.<br /> <br /> (also- am I missing something? there were 6 conspiracies on the corebook- the Aegis Kai Doru, the MM, Lucifuge, Cherion. Ascending Ones and Task Force VALKYRIE. Unless one of them is suddenly no longer considered a &quot;conspiracy&quot;- what's going on?)<br /> <br /> Another question on the subject- are the groups from the future Beast's Mortal Remains are also going to be mentioned?<br /> <br /> EDIT- as for the new setting examples, I always wondered if such settings would truly be &quot;new&quot;. Malta, Berlin, Vietnam and other settings have all hinted about potential Hunter crossover (not to mention Tokyo. Hototogisu- come at me!). Maybe instead of brand new settings, we'll get to see how hunters operate in places already ruled by monsters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 01-20-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:02:53-08:00","id":1035257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035245#post1035245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT- as for the new setting examples, I always wondered if such settings would truly be &quot;new&quot;. Malta, Berlin, Vietnam and other settings have all hinted about potential Hunter crossover (not to mention Tokyo. Hototogisu- come at me!). Maybe instead of brand new settings, we'll get to see how hunters operate in places already ruled by monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked this &quot;Do chapters five and/or six include cities around the world the way the other 2nd ed books do?&quot; on the blog post, to which Monica replied:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See above: we are taking an integrated approach to the worldbuilding. HTV2E will be a little different, and this is very exciting for us! Loads of setting to explore! </div> </div> </div>Which I think may mean example settings are presented within the writeups of the example monsters and mysterious places.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:05:02-08:00","id":1035258,"title":"","content":"Can I just say how amped I am to see VASCU in core? I love them so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:27:06-08:00","id":1035271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035240#post1035240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were six: Aegis kai Doru, Ascending Ones, Cheiron Group, Lucifuge, Malleus Maleficarum, and TFV.<br /> <br /> Edited to add: or should I take this to mean that one of them isn't being removed, but altered into a compact?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! This is just me not having enough coffee. No worries!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:27:29-08:00","id":1035272,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to this, it looks great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:46:39-08:00","id":1035279,"title":"","content":"so what does people think about the Council of Bones? While we only have a basic concept for them, but people who summon the ghosts of the dead to track down their killers is an awesome concept, especially since it is going to work out so well for the Slasher chronicles. Also- for a change, summoning a spirit using an Ouija board is a good idea!<br /> <br /> Another thing I hope to see is at least few new example Cabals in the Slasher section (please not the Abbey), as I've always found their concept as both fascinating and creepy as hell. Talking about Slashers- I'm not really sure how I feel about &quot;something&quot; making them. We still have to see what it actually means, but I hope it won't turn out as making Slashers as having excuse for being monsters. Slashers becoming what they are out of their own actions and choices is what makes Slashers scary for me, using the &quot;devil made me do it&quot; as an excuse for what they do. If the devil really made them do it, than they are not responsible for what they are, and it makes them a lot less scary, to me at least. But once again, we'll have to wait and see what the Outline actually meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:11:17-08:00","id":1035293,"title":"","content":"Ashwood Abbey will be one of the short Compact writeups, not a slasher group.<br /> <br /> Slashers will remain morally culpable for their actions, but, at the same time, there are more of them than there used to be, and finding out why will be a legit campaign focus. Monica and I specifically intend that there won't be a &quot;Slasher Force&quot; or some other kind of metaphysical phenomenon that just spawns slashers willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> (One thing that's a bit challenging about slashers is that, in 1e, they straddled a line between being procedural-inspired serial killers and horror-movie-inspired spree murderers. When that worked, they were a monster spin with a particular CofD flavor. When it didn't, they just kinda failed to make sense. We're conscious of that tension, and Monica's pitch was to include a variety of examples.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:15:35-08:00","id":1035297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035293#post1035293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ashwood Abbey will be one of the short Compact writeups, not a slasher group.<br /> <br /> Slashers will remain morally culpable for their actions, but, at the same time, there are more of them than there used to be, and finding out why will be a legit campaign focus. Monica and I specifically intend that there won't be a &quot;Slasher Force&quot; or some other kind of metaphysical phenomenon that just spawns slashers willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> (One thing that's a bit challenging about slashers is that, in 1e, they straddled a line between being procedural-inspired serial killers and horror-movie-inspired spree murderers. When that worked, they were a monster spin with a particular CofD flavor. When it didn't, they just kinda failed to make sense. We're conscious of that tension, and Monica's pitch was to include a variety of examples.)</div> </div> </div> </div>that sounds quit interesting. I'm excited to see how it would turn out. Thank you for replying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:27:08-08:00","id":1035330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035293#post1035293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ashwood Abbey will be one of the short Compact writeups, not a slasher group.<br /> <br /> Slashers will remain morally culpable for their actions, but, at the same time, there are more of them than there used to be, and finding out why will be a legit campaign focus. Monica and I specifically intend that there won't be a &amp;quot;Slasher Force&amp;quot; or some other kind of metaphysical phenomenon that just spawns slashers willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> (One thing that's a bit challenging about slashers is that, in 1e, they straddled a line between being procedural-inspired serial killers and horror-movie-inspired spree murderers. When that worked, they were a monster spin with a particular CofD flavor. When it didn't, they just kinda failed to make sense. We're conscious of that tension, and Monica's pitch was to include a variety of examples.)</div> </div> </div> </div> So like some isn't making slashers, so much as someone is making creating an environment that makes it easier for hunters to fall into becoming slashers, basically an enabler instead of a creatorof slashers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:41:05-08:00","id":1035340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corebook Outline &amp; Kick-off</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fiction: We\u2019re presenting the fiction as stand-alone pieces called \u201ccase files.\u201d They\u2019ll be highlighting different aspects of the setting, and they\u2019ll precede several chapters in the book. Lots of fresh monsters and locations here!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corebook Outline &amp; Kick-off</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter 5: Monsters Around The World \u2013 Every hunter needs a monster to fight, right? This is where we\u2019ll have your monster-hunting needs covered! Our approach to the monsters is to focus on urban legends around the globe, while remaining true to core monster archetypes (e.g. the vampire, poltergeist, etc.). We will offer NPCs, a section on how to create your own monsters, and a heap of Dread Powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm excited to see that Hunter sets off the beaten track when it comes to monsters. I've always felt that the game did its best either when presenting something new or when putting a spin on an old archetype. Trying to transport Splats from other gamelines always risked retreading published material, while posing a challenge in preserving nuance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corebook Outline &amp; Kick-off</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter 6: Mysterious Places \u2013 Have you ever wondered what would happen if hunters encountered a sentient haunted house? How would they cleanse a supernaturally-charged site? We\u2019re attaching rules to places where hunters fight in exciting and (hopefully) scary ways! More on this as the systems and setting development comes together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a wellspring of potential. It's fun to throw Hunters against something they can't fight directly - it forces them to be creative. I hope the book also touches on such things as curses, corrupted Relics and Twilight Zone phenomena - all to make Hunters' life unpredictable. Still, supernatural places alone add a lot to the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corebook Outline &amp; Kick-off</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter 8: Storytelling \u2013 In addition to helping Storytellers best run your games, we\u2019re also including a \u201cCreating a Compact\u201d and \u201cCreating a Conspiracy\u201d section to help you create new setting material that\u2019s in line with our rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! You're doing more than just providing gaming tools. You're making a statement about the world, that published groups don't have a monopoly on the Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:35:33-08:00","id":1035455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035279#post1035279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so what does people think about the Council of Bones? While we only have a basic concept for them, but people who summon the ghosts of the dead to track down their killers is an awesome concept, especially since it is going to work out so well for the Slasher chronicles. Also- for a change, summoning a spirit using an Ouija board is a good idea!<br /> <br /> Another thing I hope to see is at least few new example Cabals in the Slasher section (please not the Abbey), as I've always found their concept as both fascinating and creepy as hell. Talking about Slashers- I'm not really sure how I feel about &quot;something&quot; making them. We still have to see what it actually means, but I hope it won't turn out as making Slashers as having excuse for being monsters. Slashers becoming what they are out of their own actions and choices is what makes Slashers scary for me, using the &quot;devil made me do it&quot; as an excuse for what they do. If the devil really made them do it, than they are not responsible for what they are, and it makes them a lot less scary, to me at least. But once again, we'll have to wait and see what the Outline actually meant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like the &quot;Slasher Creators&quot; will be figures like Y from <i>Slashers; </i>the Fausts of the serial killer world, that pave a path that others choose to walk down. Which is all fine and dandy, as Y is one of my favorites (zhe's a psychic gestalt turned Lex Luthor-esque crime lord who wants to save humanity by creating the ultimate warriors from it, that's awesome in and of itself).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T06:28:04-08:00","id":1035694,"title":"","content":"Well, now I'm totally stoked!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>Chapter 5: Monsters Around The World</i></b> \u2013 Every hunter needs a monster to fight, right? This is where we\u2019ll have your monster-hunting needs covered! Our approach to the monsters is to focus on urban legends around the globe, while remaining true to core monster archetypes (e.g. the vampire, poltergeist, etc.). We will offer NPCs, a section on how to create your own monsters, and a heap of Dread Powers </div> </div> </div>If I may ask, will Hunter 2e work with the assumption that the monsters hunters will fight are as described in the other lines (even if statted with Dread Powers), or will we have &quot;generic baddies&quot; (as in, vampires are not necessarily Kindred, werewolves Uratha, and so on)?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:04:33-08:00","id":1035759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SNESferatu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035694#post1035694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now I'm totally stoked!<br /> <br /> If I may ask, will Hunter 2e work with the assumption that the monsters hunters will fight are as described in the other lines (even if statted with Dread Powers), or will we have &amp;quot;generic baddies&amp;quot; (as in, vampires are not necessarily Kindred, werewolves Uratha, and so on)?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume so. 1e was pretty adamant that vampires didn't have to be Kindred and encouraged you to get weird with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T15:19:17-08:00","id":1035860,"title":"","content":"I'm expecting the &quot;something or someone&quot; creating more Slashers and making them a bigger problem to be closer to a poorly understood creepy phenomenon or a consequence of how hunters have changed over the years. Truth be told I'm somewhat ambivalent because I really don't think they need a face or group spreading their numbers to be an unavoidable out-of-the-box problem disconcertingly close to the player splat, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> I'm pumped to find out how the Code will look, and a book full of monsters and unsettling locales to investigate sounds great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-21-2017, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:48:09-08:00","id":1035891,"title":"","content":"I'm a little sad we aren't going to see the same city structure that other 2e corebooks had. Those writeups are so fun, and would be a great chance for some regional organizations to pop up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T22:20:15-08:00","id":1035957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035101#post1035101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the same token, it would make a lot of sense for Ashwood to be the Compact that gets cut if it's featuring in the Slasher Chronicle chapter. Which I would certainly hope it does, what with the Hunt Club being part of them and all. I would have assumed Ashwood would be the Compact to VASCU's Conspiracy in that chapter, if it hadn't been specified that the Compact was new and as of yet unnamed. So I'm guessing they've gone full black hat. But it's possible the new Compact could be an Abbey offshoot, the rest having been corrupted by the Hunt Club.</div> </div> </div> </div>When was it said the Hunt Club was a part of Ashwood Abbey? As far as I was aware they were both distinct hellfire clubs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T22:46:04-08:00","id":1035964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035957#post1035957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When was it said the Hunt Club was a part of Ashwood Abbey? As far as I was aware they were both distinct hellfire clubs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably just me misremembering things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T22:53:05-08:00","id":1035965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035957#post1035957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When was it said the Hunt Club was a part of Ashwood Abbey? As far as I was aware they were both distinct hellfire clubs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was brought up by the developer in an earlier post about reconsidering the topic. Combining the two was on the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slashers-and-ashwood-abbey/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slashers-and-ashwood-abbey/\" target=\"_blank\"> Hunter 2E Open Dev: Slashers and Ashwood Abbey &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slashers-and-ashwood-abbey/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slashers-and-ashwood-abbey/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-22-2017, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T22:58:24-08:00","id":1035967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035860#post1035860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm expecting the &quot;something or someone&quot; creating more Slashers and making them a bigger problem to be closer to a poorly understood creepy phenomenon or a consequence of how hunters have changed over the years. Truth be told I'm somewhat ambivalent because I really don't think they need a face or group spreading their numbers to be an unavoidable out-of-the-box problem disconcertingly close to the player splat, but we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because each 'XYZ Chronicles' parts of 2E corebook need to be easy structure for creating... well, <i>chronicle</i>, with recognized antagonists. Strix are there to rise stacks ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) in <b>Vampire</b>, Idigam are to make disconcerting, hardened 'master hunters' of <b>Werewolf</b> something to rumble and be terrified about - and to stir Shadow to make more possible to see all this collections of enemies on PCs pack territory in the first place - and Fallen World is constant Obsession of mages ( this one, in POV is worst at fulfilling this ' XYZ Chronicle' purpose ). Firestorms in <b>Promethean</b> are made to 'move your asses' for characters that stop their Pilgrimage or just to make more story hooks when chronicle goes on semi-hiatus - there is nothing more energizing like magical storm that rise dead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Huntsmans in <b>Changeling</b> are constant threat that is much more plausible than True Fae coming from Arcadia always working to recapture their ex-slaves.<br /> <br /> In that light, Slashers in <b>Hunter</b> <i>need</i> to be more than some random killer or two, coming from <i>something </i>that is main mystery of particular game. Other way around, <b>Hunter</b> chronicles would have no 'main plot' and be just series of Monsters of the Week, not connected to main arc that characters should really care. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm more the guy for having each Slashers being unique phenomena, but I'm understanding <i>why</i> they need some source that is connecting them in to larger narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-22-2017, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T23:15:20-08:00","id":1035970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035965#post1035965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was brought up by the developer in an earlier post about reconsidering the topic. Combining the two was on the table.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slashers-and-ashwood-abbey/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-ope...ashwood-abbey/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I would miss dearly Ashwood Abbey if they would be cut out - I'm concerned with their over-sexualization in 1E sources, but they, as group, adding something <i>vital</i> to <b>Hunter</b> game - group that is there just for thrill, not some great scheme or 'noble purpose'. If they would be cut out, some other group should fill the niche.<br /> <br /> I would see Abbey as 2E example of Slashers infiltration of Compacts and that many Hunt Club members are ex-Abbey - but just so with many from others Conspiracies and Compacts. Ashwood Abbey is not 'evil' on itself, they just want to have some fun with hunting monsters. Problem was that their were made too much about sexual violence in 1E, that was really unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T01:48:58-08:00","id":1035981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035965#post1035965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was brought up by the developer in an earlier post about reconsidering the topic. Combining the two was on the table.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slashers-and-ashwood-abbey/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-ope...ashwood-abbey/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That would really disappoint me to be honest; I always felt that Ashwood Abbey held an important philosophy when it came to the vigil; like how the Loyalists of Thule sought redemption and how the Null Mysteriis sought knowledge, each of the compacts had their own philosophical reason for the vigil. The Abbey's philosophy was that it was all too much fun, and I felt like that'd be a philosophy more than a few hunters would share. Of course I didn't like how they were depicted as absolute freaking monsters at times, but I was hoping that would change in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T02:28:58-08:00","id":1035988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035981#post1035981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would really disappoint me to be honest; I always felt that Ashwood Abbey held an important philosophy when it came to the vigil; like how the Loyalists of Thule sought redemption and how the Null Mysteriis sought knowledge, each of the compacts had their own philosophical reason for the vigil. The Abbey's philosophy was that it was all too much fun, and I felt like that'd be a philosophy more than a few hunters would share. Of course I didn't like how they were depicted as absolute freaking monsters at times, but I was hoping that would change in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>don't worry. Rose has just clarified it would not be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T02:30:53-08:00","id":1035990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035988#post1035988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">don't worry. Rose has just clarified it would not be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, where she wrote that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T04:21:40-08:00","id":1036018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035279#post1035279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so what does people think about the Council of Bones? While we only have a basic concept for them, but people who summon the ghosts of the dead to track down their killers is an awesome concept, especially since it is going to work out so well for the Slasher chronicles. Also- for a change, summoning a spirit using an Ouija board is a good idea!</div> </div> </div> </div>On a meta level, I think Monica and Rose wanted the broader range of lines that have come out since the first edition to be represented in the core splats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I woudn't be surprised if the new compact has focus in common with Mummy or Deviant - or to find Habibi Ma promoted to the core).<br /> <br /> On an in-setting level, it sounds like a group that might have begun as a Sineater krewe. Interviewing the ghosts of victims to go after their killers sounds like something Advocates or Mourners might do - and the name sounds like something Sineaters would come up with. Maybe there was a such a krewe in the past; mortal hunters learned of it, decided it was a worthwhile endeavour, and set out to revive it.<br /> <br /> On an aesthetic level, I'm glad there is a group focussed on ghosts - even if they avenge ghosts rather than bust them. They also sound like a conspiracy that would work well with other hunters - perhaps even making themselves available as consultants of a sort.<br /> <br /> My biggest question is which comes first: do they come across monsters and investigate via looking for victims, come across victims and go looking for the monster, or both? If it's the second, I could easily see them not confining themselves to supernatural killers, but going after slashers or even mortal murderers. (I would like that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035990#post1035990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, where she wrote that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Previous page. Ashwood Abbey will be one of the briefly described compacts rather than a full splat, but still there and still hunters rather than slashers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T06:13:20-08:00","id":1036032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035759#post1035759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume so. 1e was pretty adamant that vampires didn't have to be Kindred and encouraged you to get weird with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought Requiem 1e itself was pretty good about Vampires not having to be Kindred and getting weird about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hoping that the new core book is going to use the Horror rules from CoD 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:01:45-08:00","id":1036952,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious about the mention of poltergeists as monsters. I wonder if that means we're going to see ghosts using the standard monster rules, instead of ephemeral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T23:15:28-08:00","id":1037059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1036952#post1036952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really curious about the mention of poltergeists as monsters. I wonder if that means we're going to see ghosts using the standard monster rules, instead of ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they finally incorporate Ephemerals rules in <b>Hunter</b>, as ghosts, spirits and even 'demons' ( those from 1E corebook ) are better run as those than 'fleshy' monsters ( by Horrors rules ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:40:09-08:00","id":1037367,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">They h</span>aven't confirmed yet which way they plan to go. <br /> In response to my question in the comments thread, Monica Valentinelli said &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">We are exploring this, since many urban legends are essentially poltergeists. Nothing has been confirmed yet, though.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, it might happen. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:08:08-08:00","id":1037889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035037#post1035037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Abbey, if I had to guess.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm an idiot. Cheiron, maybe? Especially if they're baddies in Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope not. Then we wouldn't have anyone in the &quot;hunts for profit&quot; niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:47:50-08:00","id":1037913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1035340#post1035340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes! You're doing more than just providing gaming tools. You're making a statement about the world, that published groups don't have a monopoly on the Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>just wanted to note that 1E already had a section about creating new organizations in the corebook, included with potential ideals. Also, Hunter of all other gamelines seemed to encourage making your own splats for your games, publishing new major splats (and not sub splats) in supplements and offering potential groups for readers to homebrew. The best example for this is Glimpses of the Unknown- most of the gamelines in there got something in the style of new Rite or some cool power. Hunter got new splat in the form of the Heritage House.<br /> <br /> Still, I agree that having a section about it in 2E is an important thing, especially since most of my homebrew is Hunter groups of all kinds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:09:49-08:00","id":1037963,"title":"","content":"you know, talking about the Heritage House has just made me understand how much Monica took upon herself and her team- the core book only gives us 12 splats. Each of the 4 specialist books gives us another 4- so another 12. Then we have 2 more from Slasher, 4 more from Mortal Remains to which 3 more are going to be added with the upcoming Beast chapter, Dark Eras adds 4 from Doubting Souls and 5 from Fallen Blossom. If we also include groups published from outside the regular Hunter line, we have another 3 to the mix. To this we add one new conspiracy and two new compacts- which is about 48 different groups. I don't know how &quot;sort&quot; would the sort writeups be, but even as only small paragraphs and removing some historic groups or other orgs it is still a considerable amount of wordcount and a lot of hard work.<br /> <br /> In sort, all of the Hunter fans should take a moment to say a huge &quot;thank you&quot; to Monica.<br /> <br /> talking about the sort writeups- I wonder if they would be expanded later. Having a full supplement just to update old groups or something feels a bit like a waste to me, since we already have their old versions and with the sort writeups (which may detail how to fit the new edition) and the &quot;organization building&quot; tools, I assume it is a bit redundant, and there may be better ways to spend word count. Perhaps a few would be published as blog posts, like the Gimu (which didn't got the Dark Eras) or certain Bloodlines from Vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T06:05:41-08:00","id":1039393,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious as to the extent of the &quot;tailored gameplay&quot; mentioned in Chapter 4 of the outline. Will we see more Hunter-specific mechanics to differentiate them from corebook mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T06:38:47-08:00","id":1039400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1034998-2e-outline-is-here?p=1037963#post1037963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In sort, all of the Hunter fans should take a moment to say a huge &quot;thank you&quot; to Monica.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Thankyou Monica.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T08:51:45-08:00","id":1045104,"title":"","content":"Question, for Monica, or anyone else who's read something I missed or remembers something I've forgotten. Are the slashers in 2nd edition going to have the same Undertakings, different Undertakings, or be built individually? What about the Ripper/Scourge divide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:43:14-08:00","id":1059795,"title":"","content":"I'm really exited about mysterious places since I have been planning on doing a living haunted house for awhile now. The Slasher phenomenon kind of ties in with my Homebrew world's plot hook for my monsters that Hunters are becoming more numerous than ever and humanity as a whole seemed to be catching on to more of the truth about monsters(I.E they'll be quicker to use silver on the big wolf creature, they'll know fire is good against vampires etc.) and that can be easily tied in to an influx of slashers. I hope that the &quot;creating a monster&quot; rules will have more standardized suggestions and powers for the classic archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}